The controller renders our first form:

```php
    #[Route('/profile', name: 'app_profile')]
    public function profile(Environment $twig, FormFactoryInterface $formFactory): Response
    {
        $form = $formFactory->create(ProfileType::class);

        return new Response($twig->render(
            'app/templates/form.html.twig',
            [
                'form' => $form->createView(),
            ],
        ));
    }
```

We already start creating a atomic twig structure with:

 - `templates/app/templates/form.html.twig` extending base.html.twig and call form component
 - `templates/app/organisms/form.html.twig` rendering the form
 
We also use Twig new `types` block to define our supported variables:

```twig
{%- types
    title?: 'string',
    form: 'Symfony\Component\Form\FormView',
-%}

{%- extends 'app/base.html.twig' -%}

{% block main %}
    {{ include('app/organisms/form.html.twig', { form: form }, with_context = false) }}
{% endblock %}
```

And:

```twig
{%- types
    form: 'Symfony\Component\Form\FormView',
-%}

{{ form(form) }}
```

That way we know what is required or not for a component and what a controller need to give to a template or not.

